From 6746479f30e3e676dc34a10045bf0570489185dd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Substring <frog2wah@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 18:43:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] output-configuration: custom timings
 (wlr-output-management v5)

Implement version 5 of wlr-output-management: set_custom_timings sets a
mode from exact timings (modeline), modes advertise their name and
timings, and remove_custom_mode removes a custom mode.

The timings of the modes are kept along with the output, custom modes
survive connector probes, and the KMS backend applies custom timings as
they are instead of looking for a kernel mode of the same size.

Custom modes aren't saved, like with xrandr: the last mode which isn't
custom is saved instead, so that a restart never picks a mode of the
same size with other timings, which could damage a CRT monitor.

The protocol comes from a vendored wayland-protocols-wlr with the v5
XML, until it is released.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
